From: faycal <faycalelhandi9@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:25:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/26] feat(agc): lane-separated recorder batches for async
 compute (APS5_COMPUTE_LANE)

Stage 1 of running async compute on its own Vulkan queue. With APS5_COMPUTE_LANE=1, queue workers
0x40 and 0x48 record into compute-lane batches and every other thread into graphics-lane batches:
when a thread of the other lane needs the recorder, ensureOpen submits the open batch first, so each
batch holds one lane's work, in the original order, with one command buffer as before. A thread's
lane is fixed when its queue worker starts (the GPU-lock thread tag can be retagged by waits).

Splitting a batch into per-lane command buffers mid-batch was tried first and dropped: some recording
paths keep a command buffer across a submit-and-wait and rely on the batch's buffer being reused.

Astro Bot world map: 0 validation errors (VK_LAYER_KHRONOS_validation, 200 s), screenshot correct;
render passes broken by interleaved compute 3075 -> 602 per 10 s, submits 161k -> 277k per run,
presents ~5% lower (106-122 vs 113-130 per 10 s) while both lanes share one queue. Off by default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
